      "text": "1. **Identify the points on the line:** Given the points $(4, 5)$ and $(8, 17)$ lie on the line $y = ax + b$.\n2. **Substitute the points into the line equation:**\n   - For $(4, 5)$: \n     \\[\n     5 = 4a + b \\quad \\text{(Equation 1)}\n     \\]\n   - For $(8, 17)$:\n     \\[\n     17 = 8a + b \\quad \\text{(Equation 2)}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Solve the system of equations:**\n   - Subtract Equation 1 from Equation 2 to eliminate $b$:\n     \\[\n     17 - 5 = 8a + b - (4a + b)\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     12 = 4a\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     a = 3\n     \\]\n   - Substitute $a = 3$ back into Equation 1 to find $b$:\n     \\[\n     5 = 4(3) + b\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     5 = 12 + b\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     b = 5 - 12\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     b = -7\n     \\]\n\n4. **Calculate $a - b$:**\n   \\[\n   a - b = 3 - (-7) = 3 + 7 = 10\n   \\]\n\nConclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{10}\n\\]",
