      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Since the points $(4,5)$ and $(8,17)$ lie on the line $y = ax + b$, the slope (rate of change) of the line can be found by calculating the difference in $y$ values divided by the difference in $x$ values. Therefore, the slope $a$ is given by:\n\\[a = \\frac{17 - 5}{8 - 4} = \\frac{12}{4} = 3.\\]\n\nNext, we can use the slope-intercept form $y = ax + b$ and one of the given points to solve for $b$. Using the point $(4,5)$, we substitute $x = 4$ and $y = 5$ into the equation $y = 3x + b$:\n\\[5 = 3(4) + b.\\]\nThus,\n\\[5 = 12 + b,\\]\nso\n\\[b = 5 - 12 = -7.\\]\nTherefore, $a - b = 3 - (-7) = 3 + 7 = 10$. The answer is $\\boxed{10}$.",
