      "text": "The given line $y = ax + b$ passes through the points $(4, 5)$ and $(8, 17)$. For the line to pass through $(4, 5)$, we substitute $x = 4$ and $y = 5$ into the equation to find $a$:\n\\begin{align*}\n5 &= a \\cdot 4 + b \\\\\n5 &= 4a + b.\n\\end{align*}\n\nSimilarly, for the line to pass through $(8, 17)$, we substitute $x = 8$ and $y = 17$ into the equation to find another equation involving $a$ and $b$:\n\\begin{align*}\n17 &= a \\cdot 8 + b \\\\\n17 &= 8a + b.\n\\end{align*}\n\nWe now have the following system of linear equations:\n\\begin{align*}\n5 &= 4a + b, \\\\\n17 &= 8a + b.\n\\end{align*}\n\nTo solve for $a$, we subtract the first equation from the second equation to eliminate $b$:\n\\begin{align*}\n17 - 5 &= 8a + b - (4a + b) \\\\\n12 &= 4a \\\\\na &= 3.\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow, we substitute $a = 3$ back into one of the initial equations to solve for $b$. Using $5 = 4a + b$:\n\\begin{align*}\n5 &= 4 \\cdot 3 + b \\\\\n5 &= 12 + b \\\\\nb &= 5 - 12 \\\\\nb &= -7.\n\\end{align*}\n\nThus, $a - b = 3 - (-7) = 10$.\n\nHence, the final answer is $\\boxed{10}$.",
