      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "1. **Distance Formula**: \n   First, we utilize the distance formula between two points in the plane, given by:\n   \\[\n   \\text{distance} = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}\n   \\]\n   Given the points \\((4,5)\\) and \\((8,17)\\), the distance formula yields:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{(8 - 4)^2 + (17 - 5)^2} = \\sqrt{4^2 + 12^2} = \\sqrt{16 + 144} = \\sqrt{160} = 4\\sqrt{10}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Line Equation Using Two Points**: \n   We can use the coordinates of two points to find the slope (\\(a\\)) of the line passing through them. The slope \\(a\\) is calculated as:\n   \\[\n   a = \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} = \\frac{17 - 5}{8 - 4} = \\frac{12}{4} = 3\n   \\]\n\n3. **Y-intercept \\(b\\)**:\n   Using the point-slope form of a line \\(y = ax + b\\), and substituting point \\((4, 5)\\) with \\(x = 4\\) and \\(y = 5\\):\n   \\[\n   5 = 3(4) + b \\implies 5 = 12 + b \\implies b = 5 - 12 = -7\n   \\]\n\n4. **Compute \\(a - b\\)**:\n   Finally, we find \\(a - b\\):\n   \\[\n   a - b = 3 - (-7) = 3 + 7 = 10\n   \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\nThus, the value of \\(a - b\\) is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
